        <div class="recognition-copy">
            <p class="dossier-eyebrow"><span>01</span> Recognition</p>
            <h2 id="business-recognition-title">The dispute may begin at work. The exposure often does not stay there.</h2>
            <p>A personal email may recover a company account. One phone may hold private communications, business authentication and shared storage. Browser profiles, cloud services and old permissions may cross the same boundary. Access created during years of cooperation may no longer fit the relationship.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="recognition-pull">You do not need to assume hostile access to recognize that the overlap matters.</p>
    </div>
</section>

